  "description": "Lazy, scaffold-first Blazor WebAssembly for static hosts. Generates static HTML shells for your pages at publish time with HtmlRenderer, so a visitor sees real content in under a second without downloading the .NET runtime; boots the runtime only on intent (click, visibility, idle or immediately) with a tiny loader that handles the Blazor readiness race; mounts named components as islands inside static pages, including components that live in lazy-loaded assemblies; lets components skip I/O while being prerendered (IBuildTime, NotAtBuildTime); fails the build when startup code references a lazy-assembly type; and runs C# services in a Web Worker behind a typed, awaitable interface with progress, streaming results (IAsyncEnumerable with backpressure), cooperative cancellation and terminate-and-restart for jobs that never yield.",
  "id": "EvaluatedApplications.Blazier",
